        <body>
            <div xml:id="d110">

                <pb facs="0263" n="167" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg167"/>

                <head>No. 110.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Wing.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1871-11-23"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 23,
                        1871</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 65.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch, No. 151, of the 17th ultimo,
                    in relation to the case of Doctor L. D. Wilson, has been received.</p>
                <p>With reference to his case you state: 1st. That his imprisonment was the result
                    of mistaken identity $ 2d. That it embodies a flagrant case of outrage.</p>
                <p>In reply, I have to request that you will furnish farther explanations to sustain
                    those statements.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
